From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:27:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Map the full PCIe DART register
 windows

The T8132 PCIe DARTs report version 2.2. Those keep the exception
bitmap at 0x4000 and the per-stream exception records at 0x8000, and
the driver reads both when it resets the DART at probe. A reg of 0x4000
leaves them unmapped, so the first exception read faults and the kernel
dies in the device initcalls with no output; the bootloader watchdog
resets the SoC about a minute later.

Use 0xc000, as aurora-silicon's t8132.dtsi does. The ADT describes
0x20000 for dart-apcie0 and dart-apcie2.

Tested on the Mac mini M4 (J773g): Aurora boots with 0xc000 windows on
these DARTs and every other short DART, and never boots with 0x4000.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index e694db6c24..a96d6e2c55 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -944,7 +944,7 @@
 
 		pcie0_dart: iommu@490000000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
-			reg = <0x4 0x90000000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			reg = <0x4 0x90000000 0x0 0xc000>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1232 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
@@ -954,7 +954,7 @@
 
 		pcie1_dart: iommu@491000000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
-			reg = <0x4 0x91000000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			reg = <0x4 0x91000000 0x0 0xc000>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1236 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
@@ -964,7 +964,7 @@
 
 		pcie2_dart: iommu@492000000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
-			reg = <0x4 0x92000000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			reg = <0x4 0x92000000 0x0 0xc000>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1250 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
